# The WarrenGuard engine rev that the pinned `warren-sdk` git rev (see
# native/warrend/Cargo.toml) was built against. This is the `.warrenguard-version`
# of that rev in warren-sdk-rs.
#
# The `[patch."https://github.com/WarrenBrowse/warrenguard.git"]` block in
# Cargo.toml repoints every warrenguard-* crate to the LOCAL sibling
# `../../../warrenguard`, which is NOT pinned: it follows whatever rev is checked
# out there. build.rs asserts that this expected rev is an ancestor of the
# sibling's HEAD, so a divergent or older checkout fails loudly instead of
# silently compiling the SDK against a mismatched protocol engine.
#
# Bump this in lockstep whenever you bump the consumed `warren-sdk` rev: set it to
# the new rev's `.warrenguard-version`
# (`git -C ../warren-sdk-rs show <rev>:.warrenguard-version`).
